# TechieFlow line-ending policy — this repo is consumed by bash on WSL, macOS and Linux.
# A CRLF checkout breaks every shell script ("/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r'") INCLUDING the
# .tfcore/hooks/*.sh PreToolUse guards, which then lock the AI agents out of Bash AND
# Write/Edit. "text=auto" alone is NOT enough: it normalizes the committed blobs but
# lets core.autocrlf=true (the Git-for-Windows default) smudge the working tree to
# CRLF on checkout — which is exactly what broke the scripts on 2026-07-11.
# "eol=lf" pins the WORKING TREE to LF on every platform.
#
# After changing this file, the owner runs once:
#   git add --renormalize . && git commit
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
